# Build output. Regenerated by every build; never worth committing or uploading.
bin/
obj/
.vs/

# The framework reference assemblies.
#
# These are NOT ignored. They are committed on purpose, so that this project compiles and gives
# you IntelliSense the moment somebody clones or unzips it - a model folder that opens to red
# squiggles has failed before it starts.
#
# THIS COPY IS YOURS. It was made when this project was scaffolded, and nothing refreshes it
# for you: downloading a newer Domain Model Assistant replaces the Assistant's own refs\, not
# this one, and leaves you compiling against the older framework with no error to notice.
# Refresh it from a PowerShell terminal in your Assistant folder:
#
#     .\scripts\refresh-model-refs.ps1 -Project "<full path to this project folder>"
#
# Use the script rather than copying files in by hand - it empties the folder before it fills
# it, and that matters: the reference in the .csproj is a wildcard, so an assembly left behind
# from another framework release is compiled against rather than ignored. Never edit them.
#
# jcass-dm check reports a NOTE when this folder and the Assistant's disagree.
#
# Symbols are the one thing not carried.
refs/*.pdb
